    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** and **Drake Baldwin** pairing serves as the cornerstone for today\u2019s lineup, offering the highest projected efficiency. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out with a robust 81.87 score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Elder and a potent spot in the batting order, while **Drake Baldwin** (71.82) benefits from an elite combination of a hitter-friendly park and a high-leverage leadoff opportunity. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** and **Sam Antonacci** are high-priority starts, both capitalizing on top-of-the-order usage and favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs exceeding 4.80. While **Kyle Tucker** carries a lower score of 51.41 due to a tougher matchup against McLean and a less optimal batting position, his pedigree keeps him in the starting nine as he anchors our offensive depth.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily favors favorable parks and high-xERA pitching matchups. **Heliot Ramos** is a standout value at 66.52, receiving a notable boost from an favorable wind direction, while **Nasim Nunez** provides surprisingly strong utility (61.72) despite the bottom-of-the-order assignment, largely due to a soft matchup against Bratt. The most difficult bench decision involved **Denzer Guzman**, who posted a 53.32 score; despite strong platoon indicators and wind support, his raw production projection simply could not displace the high-floor reliability offered by the starting MI and OF core. **Josh Jung** remained on the bench primarily due to the uncertainty of a \"Lineup Pending\" status and a sub-optimal matchup against the high-skill arm of Woo, ensuring we prioritize active, confirmed production over speculative upside.",
